Locate answers before drafting a research brief — learner brief
Fictional Northstar Services training material.
Questions
Where are business description, management discussion, and audited statements located? SEC historical guide: https://www.sec.gov/answers/reada10k.htm Modified 2011-07-01. Open and record access date. This is orientation, not current filing law.
Task
Northstar's new analyst needs a map of where annual-report information lives before a training session. Produce a source-location brief, without interpreting any company's results.
Actions
	1	Read the request and restate its three questions in your own words.
	2	Ask AI for a search plan and a table with one row per question; treat returned links as unverified.
	3	Open the SEC guide and locate the relevant sections yourself; record the modification date.
	4	Give the located passages or brief paraphrases to AI and ask it to populate the table without adding current requirements.
	5	Check all three citations against the original, remove unsupported claims, and add one follow-up requiring current evidence.
Output
Question; source title/URL; publisher; publication/access date; section; paraphrased answer; current-rule limitation; unresolved question.
